      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don't want to see useless hamburger menu in the corner of the screen that I will never use. I will never use it, it's like decoration that I don't want. I need my mic icon visible somehow because I am now constantly missing talking to my friends because I am muted. It's happened multiple times now, and I don't want to clutter my screen with useless icons. I need to use push to talk because my house is noisy and sometimes I hot-mic. I can't mentally keep track of whether I'm muted just by the noise of mute/un-mute. \n\nTo keep my mic indicator visible, which is a tool I actively use during every conversation I have on VRChat, I have to enable other HUD elements which I will never use. I have never had to deal with this since I started playing VRChat, 5 years ago. There has been in the past feedback from users regarding the mic icon that resulted in real improvements to its function as a tool. The current functionality of the mic icon seems like a regression on those improvements.\n\nEdit: I want to be a bit more thorough about how I rely on the mic icon. When I'm muted, it flashes red for a moment. Otherwise, it isn't displayed. The setting is Mic Icon Visibility - When Muted. This catches me right away so that I can unmute.\n\nEdit Edit: I discovered, thanks to help from open beta folks, that (as of writing this) you can enable hud>set transparency to 0>enable mic icon in audio settings to be in bottom left position> set its transparency to something visible - this will let you have bottom left mic icon with no other hud elements. Somebody mentioned this does not fix the notifications issue though.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
